{
  "content": "Hello! I’m a UK government mediation assistant. I can help you explore whether you might be eligible for benefits such as Universal Credit or Personal Independence Payment, and guide you through the application process. You don’t need to share any sensitive details right now. Could you tell me what brings you here today?",
  "source": "user_agent",
  "reply_type": "free_text",
  "actions": null
}

We need to produce ElicitationResponse. Input: content "Do you currently live in the UK?" source user_agent reply_type yes_no. expects_reply true but not needed. Since reply_type yes_no, we must create exactly two actions: Yes and No. Each action has label and payload. Payload can be same as label? Should be message to send if user chooses. Use label capitalized correctly: "Yes", "No". Payload maybe same as label. Provide actions array.

Schema: actions is array of ElicitationAction objects. So output:

{
 "content": "Do you currently live in the UK?",
 "source": "user_agent",
 "reply_type": "yes_no",
 "actions": [
   {"label": "Yes", "payload": "Yes"},
   {"label": "No", "payload": "No"}
 ]
}

Make sure no extra fields.

